# Main GameRules wProc for Noxious Bog
# Author: Kilroy
#
# Custom Enemies used:
# X   klr-fury-lr : A Fury Variant equipped with dual gatlings. Custom logic to stay at range and use PDS. Focusses Turrets.
# X  klr-mega-ds : A Mega Variant that sacrifices firepower for agility and a shield generator. Specialized in Payload dropping. Focusses the CORE.
# X  klr-quasar-jmp : A Quasar Variant with Arc Cannons and increased boost speed. Has a shield generator and repair point. Will summon klr-nova-jmp on spawn and syncronize boosts between them to get behind turrets. Focussed Turrets.
# X  klr-nova-jmp : Spawned by Quasar-JMP and equipped with an arc shotgun and increased boost speed, this unit is designed to jump with klr-nova-jmp for protection. Is fast, but doesn't have many resistances.
# X  klr-fortress-ml : Equipped with chain shotguns and slagthrowers, the Fortress ML relies on vanilla pathfinding and raw stats to overwhelm the opponent.
# X  klr-mono-hp : A Mono equipped with a repair beam. Will focus the highest HP unit on the battlefield and constantly repair.
# X  klr-atrax-emp : An Atrax equipped with long range, EMP artillery and small PDS. Will not move towards the frontline, instead focussing on powergrid complexes after travelling to map waypoints. May need RTS control.
#   klr-poly-emp : A Poly with an attached arc cannon. Very fast and devastatingly effective. Focusses powergrid.
#   klr-minke-np : [GUARDIAN] A Minke variant with a long range artillery cannon that leaves slug puddles on the ground. Stays on the outskirs. May need RTS control.
#   klr-bryde-ac: [GUARDIAN] A Bryde variant focussing on Area Denial. With a lot of PDS and an a devastating slag cannon, it spells devastation for all production complexes near the coast.
#   klr-scepter-cr : [GUARDIAN] A modified Scepter with a Fighter Bay, will constantly spawn klr-poly-emp. Has several chain shotguns, making it devastating on close engagements. Is also equipped with an Arc Cannon that will focus incoming units.
#
# Memory Cell Shared between all wProcessors that manages world events, gamerules and waypoint coordinates.
# World Events:
#   At Mid Wave, spawn the First Guardian. It will destroy a rock blocking the river, allowing water units access to the internal waters of the map. It has it's own cutscene.
#      The blast will also spawn debris blocks and some minimal, Thorium patches. 
#
# Memory Cell:
# 0-1 Waypoint 1 X/Y
# 2-3 Waypoint 2 X/Y
# 4-5 Waypoint 3 X/Y
# 6-7 Waypoint 4 X/Y
# 8-9 Waypoint 5 X/Y
# 10-11 Waypoint 6 X/Y
#
# 30 isRockBlown
#
# 40 is ID of Mega-DS spawns
# 41 is Waypoint Target for Quasar-JMP
# 42 is Waypoint Target for Atrax-EMP
#
# 50 is Quasar-JMP Regroup
# 51 is Quasar-JMP Boost


# Defines waypoints in memory cell.
write 100 cell1 0
write 80 cell1 1
write 150 cell1 2
write 50 cell1 3
write x3 cell1 4
write y3 cell1 5
write x4 cell1 6
write y4 cell1 7
write x5 cell1 8
write y5 cell1 9
write x6 cell1 10
write y6 cell1 11

write @atrax cell1 40

jump noRNGroll equal @second lastSecond
op rand quasarWaypoint 0 1
write quasarWaypoint cell1 41
op rand atraxWaypoint 0 1
write atraxWaypoint cell1 42
set lastSecond second
noRNGroll:



getblock building isMegaRepairOK 20 20
jump noRespawn equal isMegaRepairOK @repair-point
setblock block @repair-point 37 27 @crux 0 #Always have a repair point up, if destroyed it just instantly respawns.
noRespawn:

sensor doEvent switch1 @enabled
jump rockEvent equal doEvent false
set isRockDestroyed false
jump rockEvent equal @waveNumber 20
end
rockEvent:
jump doRockEvent equal isRockDestroyed false
end

doRockEvent:
    set isRockDestroyed true
    write isRockDestroyed cell1 32
    cutscene pan 110 62 0.3
    wait 0.5
    effect explosion 110 62 7 %ff8800
    wait 0.2
    effect explosion 110 62 11 %ff8800
    wait 0.2
    setrate 50
    explosion @crux 110 62 15 100 yes yes no
    effect smokeCloud 110 62 40 %777777
    effect smokeBig 110 62 30 %555555
    effect explosion 110 62 15 %ff8800
    setblock block @air 106 62 @sharded 0
